roma's Japanese dictionary

system_core.dic is modified from SudachiDict core 20261015 by Works Applications Co., Ltd.
(https://github.com/WorksApplications/SudachiDict), licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSE-2.0.txt). Its parts from UniDic and NEologd, and their terms, are in sudachi-LEGAL.txt.

roma (https://github.com/zakius/roma, dict-tool/src/main/kotlin/Slim.kt) changed it:
- Removed postal addresses: compound place names of 5 or more characters that contain
  都, 道, 府, 県, 市, 区, 町, 村 or 郡.
- Removed words that another word with the same text outranks in every context.
- Cleared normalized forms, split data (A, B, C, word structure) and synonym groups.
- Connection cost matrix: kept only the ids in use, merged identical rows and columns, and
  renumbered the ids.
- Rewrote it in roma's own binary format: shorter word entries, katakana-only strings stored
  one byte per character, the connection matrix stored as shared pieces.
